20260529.111736.710 [<ideas.........] ## Core assumptions in the formal system
20260529.111736.851 [<ideas.........] The question sits inside malvin’s checks model: `.malvin/checks` is a ordered list of shell one-liners; malvin defines
20260529.111737.013 [<ideas.........] `DEFAULT_RUST_CLIPPY` as `cargo clippy --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings -W clippy::cargo`; this repo’s
20260529.111737.188 [<ideas.........] `Cargo.toml` lives under `rust/`; the Makefile already uses `cd rust && …` for `rust-test` and `lint`; and malvin init
20260529.111737.513 [<ideas.........] discovery treats Makefile, pre-commit, and CI as authoritative signals over greenfield defaults.
20260529.111737.795 [<ideas.........] Three tensions matter for boundary exploration:
20260529.111738.191 [<ideas.........] - **Claim (evidence):** malvin’s constant includes `-W clippy::cargo`; the Makefile `lint` target does not.
20260529.111738.609 [<ideas.........] - **Claim (evidence):** `.malvin/checks` currently has `make test` but no clippy line at all.
20260529.111739.121 [<ideas.........] - **Hypothesis:** The “obvious” answer `cd rust && cargo clippy --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings -W
20260529.111739.484 [<ideas.........] clippy::cargo` is a small composition of existing pieces, so MBC2 should push past it.
20260529.111739.701 [<ideas.........] ---
20260529.111739.900 [<ideas.........] ## Idea 1 — Negate the atomic clippy line: delegate entirely to Makefile aggregation
20260529.111740.163 [<ideas.........] **Assumption challenged:** Clippy must appear as its own explicit `.malvin/checks` line.
20260529.111740.925 [<ideas.........] **Extreme:** Treat clippy the same way tests are already treated — not as a raw `cargo` invocation, but as a side effect of
20260529.111741.474 [<ideas.........] a Makefile target. This repo’s `lint` target already runs `cd rust && cargo clippy …`, then `ruff check`, then `kiss check`.
20260529.111741.882 [<ideas.........] The structurally distant move is to collapse the fragmented checks file (`kiss check`, `ruff check .`, `make test`) into a
20260529.111742.502 [<ideas.........] smaller set of make-driven gates, e.g. `make lint` plus `make test`, so clippy never appears as a standalone cargo line at
20260529.111742.663 [<ideas.........] all.
20260529.111742.902 [<ideas.........] **Negation:** There is no clippy string in `.malvin/checks`; Makefile owns Rust lint semantics.
20260529.111743.614 [<ideas.........] **Pathological edge:** If `make lint` and the individual lines diverge later (someone edits one and not the other), malvin’s
20260529.111744.354 [<ideas.........] gate surface shrinks to two targets and Rust lint strictness becomes whatever `lint:` says — currently `-D warnings` only,
20260529.111744.525 [<ideas.........] without `-W clippy::cargo`.
20260529.111744.779 [<ideas.........] ---
20260529.111744.798 [<ideas.........] ## Idea 2 — Negate `cd rust &&`: cwd-invariant invocation via `--manifest-path`
20260529.111745.229 [<ideas.........] **Assumption challenged:** The standard line must follow the Makefile’s `cd rust &&` prefix convention.
20260529.111745.834 [<ideas.........] **Extreme:** Never change directory. Run clippy from repo root using an explicit manifest path, composing malvin’s constant
20260529.111745.984 [<ideas.........] with a path anchor:
20260529.111746.164 [<ideas.........] ```text
20260529.111746.402 [<ideas.........] cargo clippy --manifest-path rust/Cargo.toml --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings -W clippy::cargo
20260529.111746.609 [<ideas.........] ```
20260529.111747.065 [<ideas.........] **Structural distance:** Same flags as `DEFAULT_RUST_CLIPPY`, but a different execution topology — no `cd`, no reliance on
20260529.111748.079 [<ideas.........] shell directory state. This is not a parameter tweak; it is a different way to bind the workspace root to the crate.
20260529.111748.451 [<ideas.........] **Asymptotic / pathological edge:** malvin, pre-commit, or CI may invoke checks from varying working directories; `cd rust
20260529.111749.039 [<ideas.........] &&` fails silently or confusingly if something has already changed cwd, while `--manifest-path` is invariant. Conversely, in
20260529.111750.575 [<ideas.........] a repo with multiple `Cargo.toml` files at different depths, manifest-path forces an explicit choice of which crate is “the”
20260529.111750.766 [<ideas.........] Rust gate — a boundary malvin’s root-`Cargo.toml` pre-commit template does not handle.
20260529.111750.964 [<ideas.........] ---
20260529.111751.167 [<ideas.........] ## Idea 3 — Invert authority: Makefile flags defeat malvin’s `DEFAULT_RUST_CLIPPY`
20260529.111751.641 [<ideas.........] **Assumption challenged:** `DEFAULT_RUST_CLIPPY` is the canonical flag tail for `.malvin/checks`.
20260529.111752.037 [<ideas.........] **Extreme:** For existing repos, discovery semantics say Makefile wins. The standard clippy line is therefore the exact
20260529.111752.400 [<ideas.........] Makefile excerpt, not malvin’s constant:
20260529.111752.535 [<ideas.........] ```text
20260529.111752.697 [<ideas.........] cd rust && cargo clippy --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings
20260529.111752.842 [<ideas.........] ```
20260529.111752.988 [<ideas.........] **Negation:** Deliberately omit `-W clippy::cargo` (and any `.cursorrules` pedantic/nursery flags) because the discovered
20260529.111753.176 [<ideas.........] local convention is weaker than malvin’s greenfield default.
20260529.111753.310 [<ideas.........] **Structural distance:** Same `cd rust && cargo clippy` shape as the naive answer, but opposite semantics — authority flows
20260529.111753.533 [<ideas.........] from Makefile discovery, not from malvin’s bundled constant. The checks file becomes a mirror of `lint:`’s first command,
20260529.111753.702 [<ideas.........] not a mirror of `DEFAULT_RUST_CLIPPY`.
20260529.111754.442 [<ideas.........] **Pathological edge:** Three authorities coexist in this repo — malvin (`-W clippy::cargo`), Makefile (no `clippy::cargo`),
20260529.111755.123 [<ideas.........] `.cursorrules` (`pedantic` + `nursery` + `cargo`). Picking Makefile-only is the boundary case where `.malvin/checks`
20260529.111755.703 [<ideas.........] intentionally disagrees with both malvin defaults and cursor coding rules, maximizing internal inconsistency while still
20260529.111755.950 [<ideas.........] obeying the checks-file formalism.
20260529.111756.155 [<ideas.........] ---
20260529.111756.309 [<ideas.........] ## tl;dr
20260529.111756.632 [<ideas.........] Three boundary answers to “what clippy line belongs in `.malvin/checks`?”: (1) don’t add one — fold Rust lint into `make
20260529.111757.260 [<ideas.........] lint` and drop atomic clippy/ruff/kiss lines; (2) skip `cd rust &&` and use `--manifest-path rust/Cargo.toml` with the full
20260529.111757.743 [<ideas.........] `DEFAULT_RUST_CLIPPY` flag tail; (3) add `cd rust && cargo clippy --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings` exactly as
20260529.111758.296 [<ideas.........] Makefile `lint` defines it, rejecting malvin’s `-W clippy::cargo`. All three stay inside malvin’s one-command-per-line
20260529.111800.272 [<ideas.........] checks system but differ structurally from the naive `cd rust &&` + `DEFAULT_RUST_CLIPPY` composition.
